  `29 D' = D - q₀`, `32 m^k`;

scratch registers `2, 6 … 18` (the level frame `2, 6 … 10`, loop registers `11 … 15`, tests
`16, 17`, the scale `18`).

* `BaseR`, `CoreR`: the register facts; `CoreR.push`: pushes on scratch registers keep them.
* `levR_frame`: a level frame on top of the core registers is a `LevR`.
* **`topQ`**: the recursive procedure `topC` implements the kernels `C` on the bits
  `i ≤ x < q₀` of the layer, by level-`0` calls.
