/-!
# Round six, item language (I3): the level procedure for a network with slot-set children

The level procedure `levCH c jL rowC` (to be placed at index `jL` of the table) implements
`tens Cm` on `E` bits (`E` on `vk`) at positions `e - K i` (`e` on `vE`), strides
`2^{e - K i} S₀`, of `B 2^t S₀` records.  Configuration `c : Cfg`: `W` data roles, `T`
temporaries, slot count `m`, gate-class bound `A`, the scale parameters `Aw`, `p`, and the
network `c.net` (the normalized network on `Fin (W + T)`, `R6IL3Net.netF`).

* `E = 0`: nothing;
* `0 < E < 2m` (`chainC`): the kernel on bit `e` (a frozen level-`0` frame and `leafC`), then the
  level call on the `E - 1` bits below;
* `E ≥ 2m` (`nodeC`): with `F = E / m`, the node registers (`nodeFr1`, `nodeFr2`), the steps of
  the network on `W + T` roles of `B/W 2^t S₀` records (temporaries allocated as zero records by
  `padCU`), the leftover `E mod m` bits (a level call), and the scale pad `scaleQ` by
  `δ = Gs E - cL - ∑ Gs (s F) - E mod m`.

A child step `child w S _` (with `S = pref m s`) pushes `wP = 2^{Gs (sF)}`, the child frame
`vX = Gs (sF)`, `vB = B/W`, `vk = s F` (`vE` unchanged: the slots `< s` are the top `s F` bits)
and runs `wrapQ` around the call.
